  "body": "Red on the Windows box (xiaomi-gpu, Windows 11, Go 1.26.8) in a full `go test -timeout 45m ./...` through win-run at main 373cab2b0 (2026-11-05). Windows CI only compiles the tests, so nothing else shows it (#1827). Unrelated to 373cab2b0, which changes only the Cursor mover's min string.\n\nPackage: internal/provider\n\n```\n--- FAIL: TestCodexUsageSaysWhy (0.01s)\n    --- FAIL: TestCodexUsageSaysWhy/network (0.00s)\n        codex_usage_words_test.go:95: said couldn't reach chatgpt.com for the usage read: dial tcp 127.0.0.1:1: connectex: No connection could be made because the target machine actively refused it.\n2026/11/05 14:25:19 copilot sign-in on github.com: GitHub gave the token; asking whose account it is\n2026/11/05 14:25:21 copilot sign-in on acme.ghe.com: GitHub gave the token; asking whose account it is\n```\n\nNot investigated: the cause. Not run: macOS or Linux (passes on CI there).\n",
