   "body": "A fix is on [the fork branch](https://github.com/skygunner/magpie/tree/fix/5341-connectex-keeps-last-quota), commit [f572e15d5](https://github.com/skygunner/magpie/commit/f572e15d5fb288df3a2db71d0d8dabbaad972144), based on ed0ab567.\n\nThe common matcher that keeps the last reading over transient failures matches connection refused/reset, but Windows' WSA wording is connectex: ... actively refused it. The branch adds that refusal wording, so the quota card keeps its last reading there as it does for the same refusal on other systems; a 401 or other account error is still said as it is.\n\nTestKeepLastAfterWindowsConnectionRefused reproduces the reported dial error verbatim through codexUsageWords and keepLast, and fails on the base. Related keep-last and usage-wording tests pass under race, along with vet and the offline nogui build; the Linux suite stays green. Not run on a real Windows machine; the exact connectex wording is taken from this report. AI-assisted implementation and review.",
